  "ink_note": "`ink` was previously derived from mean luminance, which mislabelled light-plate marks (e.g. a dark seal on a white disc) as light-ink. It is now measured on the mark itself, composited over #ffffff. All 52 marks read on light surfaces; none is inverted. Marks with a `plate` carry their own opaque background — do not add a white backing tile.",
  "reviewed": "2026-08-19",
  "shape_note": "`shape` describes the mark's silhouette so the UI can frame it without cropping: `round` = disc/seal, `wide` = wordmark wider than 1.6:1, `square` = everything else. Measured from the alpha channel, not the file's bounding box."
}
